    "align": "right",
    "imageUrl": "https://github.com/Cleo876/graphic-portfolio/blob/main/content/image_2026-09-24_172831111.png?raw=true",
    "html": "<h3 style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;\">What About Copyright Law in Jamaica?</h3><h3><div style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-family: Outfit, sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-weight: 400;\">In Jamaica, copyright is governed by the <span style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-weight: 600;\">Copyright Act of 1993</span> and is administered by the <span style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-weight: 600;\"><u style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;\">Jamaica Intellectual Property Office (JIPO)</u></span>. Grounded in international standards like the <span style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-weight: 600;\"><a href=\"https://www.wipo.int/en/web/treaties/ip/berne/index\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"font-semibold text-oxford underline decoration-[1.5px] underline-offset-[3px] hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity duration-200 cursor-pointer\">Berne Convention</a></span>, Jamaican law gives extensive protections to the island's robust creative, musical, and literary sectors.</div><div style=\"--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-family: Outfit, sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-weight: 400;\"><i>Take a look at the Copyright Act <a href=\"https://laws.moj.gov.jm/library/statute/the-copyright-act\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"font-semibold text-oxford underline decoration-[1.5px] underline-offset-[3px] hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity duration-200 cursor-pointer\">here</a>:</i></div></h3>"
  },
  {
    "id": "4kgjqjss5",
    "type": "text",
    "html": "<h3><span style=\"font-size: 1.5rem;\">What Is Protected?</span></h3><div>The Jamaican Copyright Act covers \"original works of the mind\", which are divided into distinct categories:</div><div><br></div><div><b>Literary &amp; Dramatic Works:</b> Poetry, novels, plays, sermons, and computer programs.</div><div><b>Musical Works:</b> The melodic composition and arrangements. <i>(Lyrics are legally treated as literary works)</i>.</div><div><b>Artistic Works:</b> Paintings, drawings, sculptures, maps, photographs, and architecture.</div><div><b>Broadcasts, Films, and Sound Recordings:</b> Critical protections for Jamaica's world-renowned music and film industries.</div><div><br></div><div>Protection is <b>completely automatic </b>the moment a work is fixed in a tangible form (such as written down or recorded).</div><div><br></div><div>You do not need to display the © symbol for your work to be legally protected, though doing so acts as a useful reminder to the public.</div><div>While formal registration is not mandatory under the law, creators can choose to voluntarily register their work at <b>JIPO</b> or through local collective management organizations like <b>JAMCOPY</b> to establish solid, official proof of ownership.</div>"
  },
  {
    "id": "l36gq7i63",
    "type": "media-wrap",
    "align": "left",
    "imageUrl": "https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTrDNVY-GQYwu1PuoikMv6vpv32GCf_72k0mTGBFnFIrBjuNmmPIXwcMBc&s=10",
    "html": "<h3>Importance of Copyright for Graphics Designer</h3><p>Copyright is <i>critical</i> for graphic designers because it transforms creative ideas into protected intellectual property, giving creators exclusive legal control over how their work is used, modified, and monetized. Without it, a designer's hard work could be freely duplicated, modified, or exploited by others without permission or compensation.</p><p>Understanding copyright is as essential as technical skill for anyone working in the visual arts. It protects a wide variety of assets—including <b>logos</b>, <b>digital illustrations</b>, <b>website graphics</b>, <b>marketing brochures</b>, and <b>UI/UX</b> layouts.</p>"
  },
  {
    "id": "oqhymd0n6",
    "type": "text",
    "html": "<h3>The Ultimate Clause for Independent Designers to Know: <i>Section 22(1)</i></h3><p><i></i></p><blockquote><i>\"22.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this section, the author of a protected work is the first owner of any copyright in that work unless there is an agreement to the contrary.\"</i></blockquote><div>What makes this so powerful for designers to know first and foremost is that:</div><div><b>As a <u>Freelancer</u></b>&nbsp;<b>you automatically own your work first unless you sign it away,</b>&nbsp;which is unlike many other forms of international standards, <i>(like UK or US).&nbsp;</i></div><div>This is <b>powerful</b>&nbsp;due to the fact that paying clients often assume that they automatically own the final vector file or logo because they paid for it. This section prooves that without a written assignment or transfer agreement signed by you,&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;your remain as the copyright owner</b>, and they only have an <i>implied</i>&nbsp;<i>license</i>&nbsp;to use it.</div><div><b>As an Employee</b>,&nbsp; even if you are a full-time, in-house graphic designer, Jamaican courts and legal experts emphasize that copyright does not automatically jump to your employer <b>unless your employment contract specifically states it does</b>.</div><div><br></div><div>There are other clauses and sections that as a Creative, you <b>should</b>&nbsp;make sure that you know so that your copyright claim can be validated in court. Which lends perfectly into the next section:</div>"
  },
  {
    "id": "s5irk5oyo",
    "type": "text",
    "html": "<h3>How to Register a Copyright for Enforcement?</h3><div>There is a great article that I will quote on this matter by <a href=\"https://www.globallawexperts.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"font-semibold text-oxford underline decoration-[1.5px] underline-offset-[3px] hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity duration-200 cursor-pointer\">Global Law Experts</a>.:</div><blockquote>Copyright registration Jamaica is less about a certificate, which does not exist, and more about disciplined proof: create the work, document authorship, contract clearly, keep independent dated records, and act fast against infringement. Get those habits right and your rights become <b>genuinely</b> enforceable rather than merely theoretical.&nbsp;</blockquote>"
